  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is config_019, which combines multimodal input, multiprofile, avgpool, and weighted fusion to reach the best validation accuracy and F1. The main remaining uncertainty is whether the current ResNet50 image representation is limiting performance, since image-only ResNet50 was weak while multimodal ResNet50 was strong. config_025 tests this by replacing only the image encoder with imagenet_vit_l while keeping the otherwise best-performing multimodal, multiprofile, avgpool, and weighted setup fixed. This is a clean single-variable comparison, potentially high-value if the image representation is a bottleneck, and avoids changing multiple design choices at once."
